R["findings"].append({
 "ref":"new",
 "title":"OP Stack portal upgraders can emit a deposit whose sender is the PoolManager, and op-geth and op-revm run it without nonce or code checks, as OP Mainnet governance did for another address on 2026-10-31",
 "chainIds":OP,"lens":"L2","assumptions":["A8","A6","A12"],"effect":"both","actor":"governance","severity":"high",
 "difference":"On Ethereum only a key or the contract's own code can move what a contract holds. On OP Stack chains the from field of a deposit transaction (type 0x7e) is whatever the OptimismPortal on Ethereum writes into the TransactionDeposited event, and the portal is an upgradeable proxy. op-geth skips the nonce check and the sender-has-code check for deposits (core/state_transition.go preCheck, the IsDepositTx branch returns before both checks), and op-revm handles a deposit in validate_against_state_and_deduct_caller without calling validate_account_nonce_and_code (handler.rs lines 130 to 161). A deposit from an address that holds code therefore runs as an outer call from that address. On Ethereum block 26,309,074 (2026-10-31 00:10:59 UTC) the OP Mainnet ProxyAdmin owner Safe 0x5a0aae59d09fccbddb6c6cceb07b7279367c3d2a, in transaction 0xd80476b3ec56283723804cf7bc2d96f800c81d3ebd0fea843555396ffe94f28f, upgraded the OP Mainnet portal to the unverified implementation 0x6d971b07cea5febaea8aefb827032f6a0538c9bb, emitted TransactionDeposited with from 0x5227f603c1ee34ce3c06efe6477003bdfccb2f8c, to the OP token predeploy 0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000042, and calldata transfer(0x6b1bae59d09fccbddb6c6cceb07b7279367c4e3b, 44,231,858.7 OP), and restored implementation 0x1005217ad392dc64cef501fa1777a27d42166748 in the same transaction. The recipient is the L1-to-L2 alias of the Safe. The temporary implementation hardcodes SENDER, RECIPIENT and AMOUNT and checks CALLER.",
 "mechanism":"An upgrade of the same kind with the PoolManager address as SENDER, a pooled token as target and transfer(recipient, balance) as calldata, or a native value transfer with a mint, would make the L2 execute a call whose msg.sender is the PoolManager. The token sees a transfer by its holder. Nothing in the PoolManager runs: unlock (src/PoolManager.sol:103-113), the delta accounting of take (src/PoolManager.sol:291-297) and the NonzeroDeltaCount check are bypassed, so pools, positions and ERC-6909 claims keep records of balances that are gone. On every one of the nine chains the stock portal sets from to msg.sender only when msg.sender equals tx.origin or carries a 23-byte EIP-7702 delegation, and to msg.sender plus 0x1111000000000000000000000000000000001111 otherwise, so an ordinary account cannot produce the PoolManager address: the PoolManager address on Ethereum has no code and nonce 0 on all nine chains, it is a CREATE-derived or predeploy address with no known key, and its alias preimage has no code and nonce 0.",
 "impact":"Every balance the PoolManager holds on the nine chains. Liquidity providers and claim holders would hold records that cannot be paid out. The OP Mainnet action shows the path is operational and was used within a day of the Arbitrum Security Council action recorded in F-138.",
 "preconditions":"The owner of the portal's ProxyAdmin on Ethereum: 0x5a0aae59d09fccbddb6c6cceb07b7279367c3d2a for OP Mainnet, Unichain, Ink and Soneium; 0x7bb41c3008b3f03fe483b28b8db90e19cf07595c for Base; 0x4a4962275df8c60a80d3a25faec5aa7de116a746 for Zora; 0xa4fb12d15eb85dc9284a7df0adbc8b696edbbf1d for World Chain; 0x4092a77baf58fef0309452ceacb09221e556e112 for Celo; 0xc290be56089bcc83c6993583ce2cf51a7951d45a for X Layer (eth_call owner() on each ProxyAdmin read from the EIP-1967 admin slot). No ordinary account can reach it.",
 "mitigations":"None in core. Integrators and LPs should treat the portal upgrade path of these chains as able to spend any L2 contract's balance. Monitors can watch Upgraded events on the nine portal proxies and TransactionDeposited events whose from equals the PoolManager address.",
 "coreRefs":["src/PoolManager.sol:103-113","src/PoolManager.sol:291-297","src/types/Currency.sol:40-80"],
 "sources":[
  {"url":"eth_getTransactionReceipt 0xd80476b3ec56283723804cf7bc2d96f800c81d3ebd0fea843555396ffe94f28f on https://eth.drpc.org (Geth/v10.0.0/drpc), saved in "+W+"op_portal_tx_d804.txt and op_forged_deposit_decode.txt","supports":"Upgraded to 0x6d971b07, TransactionDeposited from 0x5227f603...2f8c to 0x42...42 with transfer of 44,231,858.7 OP to the Safe alias, Upgraded back to 0x1005217a, sent by Safe 0x5a0aae59."},
  {"url":"eth_getStorageAt implementation slot of 0xbEb5Fc579115071764c7423A4f12eDde41f106Ed at blocks 26,309,073, 26,309,074, 26,430,858 and 26,430,859 on https://eth.drpc.org","supports":"0x1005217a before and after the action; 0xb20b23af from block 26,430,859."},
  {"url":"eth_getLogs Upgraded(address) on the nine portal proxies, Ethereum blocks 26,273,226 to 26,493,226, https://rpc.flashbots.net (reth/v2.6.0), saved in "+W+"upglogs_portals.json","supports":"The only upgrades in the window are the OP Mainnet action at 26,309,074 and an upgrade of OP Mainnet, Unichain, Ink and Soneium to 0xb20b23af at 26,430,859 that emits no TransactionDeposited."},
  {"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ethereum-optimism/op-geth/optimism/core/state_transition.go","supports":"preCheck returns early for IsDepositTx with the comment that there is no nonce to check and no need to check if EOA (lines 346-360); the EOA check sits under !SkipTransactionChecks for other transactions (lines 380-389)."},
  {"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/develop/rust/op-revm/src/handler.rs","supports":"Deposits return from validate_against_state_and_deduct_caller after crediting the mint and bumping the nonce, before validate_account_nonce_and_code_with_components (lines 130-172)."},
  {"url":"https://api.openchain.xyz/signature-database/v1/lookup (selectors of 0x6d971b07)","supports":"The temporary implementation exposes forceDeposit(), SENDER(), RECIPIENT(), AMOUNT(), OP_TOKEN(), PORTAL_PROXY() and PROXY_ADMIN()."}],
 "evidence":"primary"})

R["cleared"]+= [
 {"chainIds":ARB,"lens":"L2","check":"Lead L-873, tasks 1 and 2: the Inbox implementation each Arbitrum-family rollup uses today and how every externally callable function computes the sender passed to the Bridge.",
  "result":"No caller-chosen sender. Rollup contracts 0x4DCeB440 (Arbitrum One), 0x23a19d23 (Robinhood) and 0x508C173d (Elysium) return Inbox proxies 0x4dbd4fc5, 0x1a07cc4b and 0xce59f8b6 with EIP-1967 implementations 0x7c058ad1, 0x8d3b93df and 0x748c47ee. All three are verified on Sourcify (exact_match or match) with byte-identical Inbox.sol and AbsInbox.sol. The bytecode dispatchers hold 28 selectors each, all present in the verified ABI, none extra. Every message goes through _deliverToBridge, which passes applyL1ToL2Alias(sender) to enqueueDelayedMessage (Inbox.sol:317-326). sendL2Message, sendL2MessageFromOrigin, sendUnsignedTransaction, sendContractTransaction, sendL1FundedUnsignedTransaction, sendL1FundedContractTransaction, createRetryableTicket, unsafeCreateRetryableTicket, createRetryableTicketNoRefundAliasRewrite and both depositEth functions use msg.sender, which the alias then shifts. The three ToFork functions use undoL1ToL2Alias(msg.sender), so the Bridge sees msg.sender unaliased, only when msg.sender equals tx.origin and the chain id differs from the deploy-time chain id; eth_call of sendUnsignedTransactionToFork reverts with NotForked (0xa301bb06) on all three parent chains, and an unsigned EOA transaction keeps the Nitro EOA check that the PoolManager's code fails. debug_traceCall from each PoolManager's alias preimage shows enqueueDelayedMessage kind 3 with sender equal to the PoolManager for sendContractTransaction, sendUnsignedTransaction and sendL2Message, so only an account at the preimage reaches it. allowListEnabled and paused are false on all three. The Inbox source does not differ between the three chains or from the nitro-contracts main copy that cycle 18 read.",
  "source":SC+"1/0x7c058ad1d0ee415f7e7f30e62db1bcf568470a10, "+SC+"1/0x8d3b93dffff4842e7b61fb553b383db2c6bc91c6, "+SC+"999/0x748c47ee3702bd88f0906a0d655d2a35a37735f4; eth_call and debug_traceCall on https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com, https://eth.drpc.org, https://rpc.hyperliquid.xyz/evm and https://hyperliquid.drpc.org; "+W+"rollups.json, selectors.json, inbox_state.txt, tracecall.txt"},
 {"chainIds":ARB,"lens":"L2","check":"Task 3: every address in each Bridge's allowed delayed inbox list and outbox list, and whether any can enqueue a message with a sender it chooses.",
  "result":"No. Arbitrum One Bridge 0x8315177a lists delayed inboxes 0x57bd336d (RollupEventInbox, implementation 0x6d576e22) and the Inbox 0x4dbd4fc5, and outboxes 0x0b9857ae, 0x667e23ab and 0x760723cd. Robinhood Bridge 0xdf875533 lists the Inbox 0x1a07cc4b and RollupEventInbox 0xc34f4907 (implementation 0x796fee4a), and outbox 0xf0ce991e. Elysium Bridge 0x503d5721 lists the Inbox 0xce59f8b6 and RollupEventInbox 0x37c92ba3 (implementation 0xcd2fa60a), and outbox 0xec6b106d. The RollupEventInbox implementations are verified on Sourcify; their only enqueuing function rollupInitialized is onlyRollup and sends kind 11 with sender address(0) (RollupEventInbox.sol:17-23, AbsRollupEventInbox.sol:51-68). eth_call from an ordinary address reverts with ONLY_ROLLUP on all three, and Nitro rejects an Initialize message after genesis (parse_l2.go line 33-34). Outboxes reach the Bridge only through executeCall, which makes an L1 call and does not enqueue. submitBatchSpendingReport is onlySequencerInbox and becomes an ArbOS internal batch posting report transaction (parse_l2.go lines 76-80).",
  "source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OffchainLabs/nitro/master/arbos/parse_l2.go; "+SC+"1/0x6d576e220cb44c3e8ef75d0efbeb1ff041e2e4a5; "+SC+"1/0x796fee4adced1cb47a3e3d1b6925472f8fc8f1f9; "+SC+"999/0xcd2fa60afe0f7f19f15c7618e370900aaa87892d; "+SC+"1/0xfe4749061fb052c354aac65b9fb0ccd7e20d2418; "+W+"rollups.json, rollupeventinbox.txt"},
 {"chainIds":[42161],"lens":"L2","check":"Task 2, last part: whether the Arbitrum One Inbox implementation after the Security Council action of 2026-10-30 is the one in place before it, and whether the temporary implementation is still reachable.",
  "result":"Same implementation. eth_getLogs for Upgraded on the Arbitrum One Inbox, Bridge, SequencerInbox, RollupEventInbox and Robinhood's four proxies over Ethereum blocks 26,273,164 to 26,493,164 return four events, all in transaction 0xb69c81774f507d46ce776aeaed8b4d31df96dd66ce6fd05073481011835355d6 at block 26,301,886 sent through Safe 0xf06e95ef: upgrade to 0x980d1f93, MessageDelivered kind 3 with sender 0x3e2bf1ac unaliased, restore to 0x7c058ad1, repeated once. The implementation slot reads 0x7c058ad1 at blocks 26,000,000, 26,200,000, 26,290,000, 26,302,290, 26,400,000 and 26,493,000. The temporary implementation, verified on Sourcify, adds sendUnsignedTransactionOverride(..., address from) with no caller check and a comment that any gap leaves the bridge drainable, but it was live only inside that transaction. Called directly it runs in its own storage and its address is not an allowed delayed inbox, so it cannot enqueue.",
  "source":"eth_getLogs on https://rpc.flashbots.net; eth_getTransactionReceipt and eth_getStorageAt on https://eth.drpc.org; "+SC+"1/0x980d1f93fc5809c828539c46084801673fa6a859; "+W+"upglogs_eth.json, upglogs_eth_gapfill.txt, upgrades_arb1.json, sc_action_tx.json"},
 {"chainIds":ARB,"lens":"L2","check":"Task 4: the parent chain address whose alias is each chain's PoolManager, and what it would take to act from it.",
  "result":"Arbitrum One PoolManager 0x360e68fa...fb32 has preimage 0x24fd68faccca8ca495c1b759fd9eee466db9ea21, Robinhood 0x8366a39c...0951 has 0x7255a39cc670b4001a1121b8f6a443a643e3f840, both on Ethereum, and Elysium 0xE2e105d3...23F1 has 0xd1d005d3f7209a9da11f83ccf3e7398a753812e0 on HyperEVM. Each has no code, nonce 0 and balance 0. Acting from one needs its private key or a CREATE or CREATE2 deployment that lands on that fixed 160-bit address, a second-preimage search of about 2^160 work. HyperEVM system transactions come only from 0x2222222222222222222222222222222222222222 and the 0x20-prefixed token system addresses, so HyperCore cannot produce a transaction from the Elysium preimage. The Robinhood PoolManager address also holds 24,009 bytes of code on Ethereum with nonce 1; a contract cannot be tx.origin, so it would be aliased like any contract.",
  "source":"eth_getCode, eth_getTransactionCount, eth_getBalance on https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com and https://rpc.hyperliquid.xyz/evm; https://hyperliquid.gitbook.io/hyperliquid-docs/for-developers/hyperevm/hypercore-less-than-greater-than-hyperevm-transfers; "+W+"alias.txt"},
 {"chainIds":OP,"lens":"L2","check":"Lead L-878 and task 5: how the deployed OptimismPortal on each of the nine chains computes the from field of a deposit, and whether an ordinary account can make it equal the PoolManager.",
  "result":"No for ordinary accounts. Five implementations are in use: 0xb20b23af (version 6.1.0; OP Mainnet, Unichain, Ink, Soneium), 0x03863ab7 (6.0.1; Base), 0xe89f13c5 (5.6.1; Zora, World Chain), 0x2c431080 (5.1.1; Celo) and 0xa0fefc3a (5.2.0; X Layer), each matching SystemConfig.optimismPortal(). 0x03863ab7, 0xe89f13c5 and 0xa0fefc3a are verified on Sourcify: depositTransaction (and depositERC20Transaction on X Layer) sets from to msg.sender and replaces it with applyL1ToL2Alias(msg.sender) unless EOA.isSenderEOA(), which is msg.sender == tx.origin or 23 bytes of code starting 0xEF0100. 0xb20b23af and 0x2c431080 are not on Sourcify; their bytecode carries the same markers (PUSH20 0x1111...1111 before the TransactionDeposited topic, ORIGIN, PUSH3 0xEF0100), and their extra selectors are deleteProvenWithdrawal (0xba93107d) and setGasPayingToken. debug_traceCall shows from equal to an EOA caller on all nine, and from equal to the aliased L1CrossDomainMessenger when called through L1StandardBridge.bridgeETH on OP Mainnet, Base, Unichain, Zora, World Chain, Ink and Soneium. Celo's second TransactionDeposited site uses the fixed sender 0xdeaddeaddeaddeaddeaddeaddeaddeaddead0001 and the L1Block target behind a CALLER check against the stored SystemConfig. The PoolManager address of each chain has no code and nonce 0 on Ethereum, and so does its alias preimage; reaching either needs a key for a fixed address. EIP-3541 stops a deployed contract from having code that starts with 0xEF, so the delegation test cannot be met by a contract.",
  "source":SC+"1/0x03863ab7f64b733cff85c8ff44a86601c568ca70; "+SC+"1/0xe89f13c5ee4033b2d3cd76c9d6958efbfe26d3c2; "+SC+"1/0xa0fefc3a457f6a1ae2d81fc172d6de090a9f4033; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry/main/superchain/configs/mainnet/op.toml (and unichain, zora, worldchain, ink, soneium, celo); https://docs.base.org/base-chain/network-information/base-contracts; debug_traceCall on https://eth.drpc.org; "+W+"portals.json, bytescan.json, op_deposit_traces.json, op_deposit_traces_retry.txt, op_celo_bridge_trace.txt"},
 {"chainIds":ARB,"lens":"L2","check":"Messages that credit the PoolManager address without running its code: depositEth with the PoolManager as destination, and retryable tickets naming it as excessFeeRefundAddress or callValueRefundAddress.",
  "result":"Gift only. An EOA caller of depositEth credits its own address (Inbox.sol:202-214), and refund addresses only receive value. A native balance rise is not credited to anyone, because native settlement credits msg.value and does not read the balance (src/PoolManager.sol:350-355).",
  "source":"src/PoolManager.sol:350-355; "+SC+"1/0x7c058ad1d0ee415f7e7f30e62db1bcf568470a10"},
 {"chainIds":[42161],"lens":"L2","check":"The Arbitrum One Bridge implementation 0xfe474906 differs from the Robinhood and Elysium Bridge source.",
  "result":"The difference is a pinpoint blacklist in executeCall that reverts with CallNotAllowed when keccak256(to, data[:36]) equals one fixed hash. It applies to L2-to-L1 outbox executions on Ethereum and does not touch message enqueueing or the L2 sender.",
  "source":SC+"1/0xfe4749061fb052c354aac65b9fb0ccd7e20d2418 (src/bridge/AbsBridge.sol executeCall)"},
]

