 {"chainIds":[99901],"lens":"L2","question":"Has the Elysium Inbox or Bridge on HyperEVM ever pointed at an implementation other than 0x748c47ee and 0xc0399320? Scan Upgraded events on 0xce59f8b6, 0x503d5721, 0x37c92ba3 and 0x7f3ff53a from their creation block in 1,000-block windows, or read an explorer.",
  "why":"rpc.hyperliquid.xyz returns current code for block 1, so its historical state reads are not archive reads and the implementation samples taken this cycle prove nothing about the past. A temporary override like the Arbitrum and OP actions would be the same governance-level path.","priority":"low"},
 {"chainIds":[10,130,57073,1868,42220],"lens":"L2","question":"Obtain verified source for portal implementations 0xb20b23af (OP Mainnet, Unichain, Ink, Soneium) and 0x2c431080 (Celo), from Etherscan or the op-contracts release tag that reports versions 6.1.0 and 5.1.1, and confirm that no function other than depositTransaction, depositERC20Transaction and setGasPayingToken emits TransactionDeposited.",
  "why":"These two were read from bytecode markers and traces only. A function with a caller-chosen from would let an ordinary account move every PoolManager balance on four chains.","priority":"medium"},
 {"chainIds":[4326,137,56,43114,143,4217,5042,999,1],"lens":"L2","question":"For the nine networks outside the Arbitrum and OP families, list every protocol path that creates a transaction or call with a from field chosen outside the EVM (MegaETH deposits, Polygon state sync, Tempo and Arc system transactions, HyperEVM system transactions, Avalanche and BSC system contracts), and name who controls it.",
  "why":"The Arbitrum and OP actions of 2026-10-30 and 2026-10-31 show that these paths are used in practice. Any of them that an ordinary account can steer would move pooled balances without unlock.","priority":"medium"},
