R["leadResults"]+= [
 {"leadId":"L-873","outcome":"cleared","answer":"The deployed Inbox implementations of Arbitrum One (0x7c058ad1), Robinhood Chain (0x8d3b93df) and Elysium (0x748c47ee) are verified, share one source, and alias every sender in _deliverToBridge; the only unaliased path is the ToFork family, which reverts with NotForked on all three parent chains. The Arbitrum One implementation after the 2026-10-30 action is the one in place before it. The extra delayed inboxes are RollupEventInbox contracts that only the rollup can call, with sender address(0)."},
 {"leadId":"L-878","outcome":"finding","answer":"On all nine OP Stack chains the portal's ProxyAdmin owner can upgrade the portal to emit a deposit from any address, and op-geth and op-revm run deposits without nonce or code checks. OP Mainnet governance did this on Ethereum block 26,309,074 to move 44,231,858.7 OP from 0x5227f603...2f8c. Recorded as a governance-level finding with the upgraders of each chain. Ordinary accounts cannot set the from field to the PoolManager on any of the nine deployed portals."},
]
